  faqs: [
    { question: "How do I find an IB tutor in Bahadurgarh?", answer: "Give IB Gram your child's IB programme, subject, level and exam session, and we shortlist people who teach that exact course. As no Bahadurgarh school runs the IB, matching follows syllabus fit across the country and not location, and the lesson time is settled afterwards. A free trial lesson precedes any decision, and another tutor is offered if the fit is off." },
    { question: "Do you offer IGCSE tutors in Bahadurgarh for Cambridge or Edexcel?", answer: "Yes. Tutors matched for Bahadurgarh teach either the Cambridge or Edexcel syllabus, delivered as online tuition and not as a household visit. Matching is by exact code and tier, so a Mathematics 0580 Extended student or an Edexcel Higher-tier student gets someone who has taught that specification." },
    { question: "Do your tutors visit homes in Bahadurgarh?", answer: "No. Tutors do not visit homes in Bahadurgarh. In-person tuition runs only in Gurugram and parts of Delhi NCR, and Bahadurgarh lies outside that service area although it borders Delhi. Every lesson is live online, one to one, with a shared screen, which is real tuition from home and not a promise that anyone will arrive at your door." },
    { question: "Is Bahadurgarh part of IB Gram's home tuition network since it is so close to Delhi?", answer: "No, and it is worth saying plainly. In-person tutoring covers Gurugram and parts of Delhi NCR only. Bahadurgarh, roughly 21 kilometres from the Delhi border, is not currently in that network. Every family here works with a tutor online and never through a home visit." },
    { question: "What does an IB or IGCSE tutor in Bahadurgarh cost?", answer: "Rates move with the programme and level, the subject, how long each session runs and how lately the tutor has taught that very syllabus. Your quote arrives in writing before the trial. Diploma HL work generally sits above IGCSE Core support. Because teaching is online there is no travel element anywhere in the price, and nothing binds you beyond the sessions you choose to book." },
    { question: "Which schools do Bahadurgarh IB and IGCSE families actually study at?", answer: "No school inside Bahadurgarh currently runs the IB Diploma, Middle Years or Primary Years Programme, or Cambridge or Edexcel IGCSE. Families tied to these curricula usually study at a school in Gurugram or Delhi, both a short drive away, or occasionally Sonipat, while the town's own schools run HBSE and CBSE only." },
    { question: "My child commutes daily to a Gurugram or Delhi school from Bahadurgarh. Can a tutor work around that?", answer: "Yes, and it is among the most frequent requests tied to Bahadurgarh. Sessions are set around the real commute and the school's timetable, usually early evening once the child is home, with weekend slots for longer revision blocks before mocks or an exam series." },
    { question: "Is there a free trial lesson before I commit?", answer: "There is, for every new match. Your child takes a live online lesson on something from their own course, and it costs nothing. Afterwards the tutor sends a brief plan for the first month. Then it is your call: go ahead, ask for adjustments, or ask to meet a different tutor instead." },
    { question: "Can a tutor help with IB Internal Assessments for a child connected to Bahadurgarh?", answer: "Guidance yes, authorship no. A tutor can help your child settle on a research question that is feasible, unpack what each criterion pays for, plan how data will be gathered and respond frankly to a draft. Drafting or rewriting the assessed piece itself would breach IB academic integrity rules, which is why our tutors refuse it." },
    { question: "Which IB Diploma subjects can you help with for a Bahadurgarh family?", answer: "Most Diploma subjects are covered. Requests cluster around Maths in both flavours, Analysis and Approaches and Applications and Interpretation, at HL or SL, then Physics, Chemistry, Biology, Economics, Business Management, English A and Computer Science. Theory of Knowledge coaching and Extended Essay guidance sit alongside them." },
    { question: "Do you tutor IB MYP and PYP students connected to Bahadurgarh, not only the Diploma?", answer: "We do. Younger IB pupils are welcome, wherever they attend school. For Middle Years students the emphasis falls on criterion-by-criterion analysis and keeping a Personal Project journal that tells a coherent story. Primary Years pupils get reading, writing and number confidence, plus early practice at researching for the Exhibition." },
    { question: "Is online tutoring as effective as in-person tuition for IB or IGCSE students in Bahadurgarh?", answer: "For this town it holds up well, mainly because nobody local teaches these syllabuses at all. Screen-shared papers, a whiteboard both people can write on and saved recordings of worked solutions reproduce most of what a tutor at the desk would offer. The gain is reach: the tutor can be the best fit in India, not merely the closest." },
    { question: "How are IB Gram tutors verified for Bahadurgarh students?", answer: "Before any introduction we look at each tutor's qualifications, how recently they taught the specific subject and level, and how they handle assessment criteria. Bahadurgarh has no IB or IGCSE school to lean on, so we favour people with fresh classroom experience of the syllabus over general tutors. Your own verdict comes from the trial lesson." },
    { question: "When should my child in Bahadurgarh start IB or IGCSE tutoring?", answer: "The best moment is the start of the course: Class 11 for the IB Diploma, Grade 9 for IGCSE. That leaves room to repair weak foundations before internal exams, IA deadlines and predicted grades begin to count. Beginning in the last year is still worthwhile when lessons target the highest-value topics and past papers ahead of the series." },
    { question: "My child is switching from HBSE or CBSE to IGCSE, moving out of Bahadurgarh's local schools. Can a tutor help?", answer: "Yes, and the town sees this often, since every local school runs HBSE or CBSE only. The gap is usually question style and not content: command words such as explain, evaluate and justify need direct teaching, ideally a term before the switch." },
    { question: "Can sessions happen on weekends or after school hours for a Bahadurgarh family?", answer: "Yes, most households take weekday evenings once the commute or school day ends, plus weekend mornings for longer revision blocks. Timing allows for winter fog on the NH9 corridor, when earlier evenings are often preferred, and for Diwali and the late-December break. A second weekly slot before mocks is easy to add online." },
    { question: "What happens if we are not happy with the tutor in Bahadurgarh?", answer: "Just let us know and a new tutor is found. Every few weeks we review how things are going, and if the fit is poor we re-match instead of asking your child to soldier on. Nothing is locked in, so a pause or a full stop costs you nothing." },
    { question: "Is IB Gram affiliated with any Bahadurgarh, Gurugram or Delhi school, or with the IB or Cambridge?", answer: "No. IB Gram is an independent tutoring platform. It has no partnership with, backing from or authority over any school named on this page, the International Baccalaureate Organization, Cambridge Assessment International Education or Pearson Edexcel. Schools appear only to show where Bahadurgarh children study, and tutors follow each school's calendar and the board's published syllabus." },
  ],

